081\u2084O\u2082Cl = 11(12.0000000) + 14(1.0078250) + 2(15.9949146) + 1(34.9688527)\n= 132.0000000 + 14.109550 + 31.9898292 + 34.9688527\n= 213.0682319\n\nThis is about 2 mass units too high.\n\nLet me try C\u2081\u2080H\u2081\u2085O\u2082Cl:\nC\u2081\u2080H\u2081\u2085O\u2082Cl = 10(12.0000000) + 15(1.0078250) + 2(15.9949146) + 1(34.9688527)\n= 120.0000000 + 15.117375 + 31.9898292 + 34.9688527\n= 202.0760569\n\nThis is about 9 mass units too low.\n\nThe mass 211.07639 is between these two. Let me try formulas with different oxygen content:\n\nC\u2081\u2081H\u2081\u2085OCl:\nC\u2081\u2081H\u2081\u2085OCl = 11(12.0000000) + 15(1.0078250) + 1(15.9949146) + 1(34.9688527)\n= 132.0000000 + 15.117375 + 15.9949146 + 34.9688527\n= 198.0811423 (too low)\n\nC\u2081\u2082H\u2081\u2085OCl:\nC\u2081\u2082H\u2081\u2085OCl = 12(12.0000000) + 15(1.0078250) + 1(15.9949146) + 1(34.9688527)\n= 144.0000000 + 15.117375 + 15.9949146 + 34.9688527\n= 210.0811423 (very close! off by about 0.995)\n\nC\u2081\u2082H\u2081\u2086OCl:\nC\u2081\u2082H\u2081\u2086OCl = 12(12.0000000) + 16(1.0078250) + 1(15.9949146) + 1(34.9688527)\n= 144.0000000 + 16.12520 + 15.9949146 + 34.9688527\n= 211.0889673 (very close! off by about 0.013)\n\nThis looks like the best match! C\u2081\u2082H\u2081\u2086OCl gives 211.0889673, which is very close to the observed 211.07639 (difference of about 0.012).\n\nActually, let me double-check my calculation:\nC\u2081\u2082H\u2081\u2086OCl = 12(12.0000000) + 16(1.0078250) + 1(15.9949146) + 1(34.9688527)\n= 144.0000000 + 16.1252000 + 15.9949146 + 34.9688527\n= 211.0889673\n\nThe difference is 211.0889673 - 211.07639 = 0.0125773, which is quite small but not perfect.\n\nLet me also check C\u2081\u2081H\u2081\u2086O\u2082Cl:\nC\u2081\u2081H\u2081\u2086O\u2082Cl = 11(12.0000000) + 16(1.0078250) + 2(15.9949146) + 1(34.9688527)\n= 132.0000000 + 16.1252000 + 31.9898292 + 34.9688527\n= 215.0838819 (too high)\n\nAnd C\u2081\u2080H\u2081\u2086O\u2083Cl:\nC\u2081\u2080H\u2081\u2086O\u2083Cl = 10(12.0000000) + 16(1.0078250) + 3(15.9949146) + 1(34.9688527)\n= 120.0000000 + 16.1252000 + 47.9847438 + 34.9688527\n= 219.0787965 (too high)\n\nLet me try C\u2081\u2082H\u2081\u2085OCl again more carefully:\nC\u2081\u2082H\u2081\u2085OCl = 12(12.0000000) + 15(1.0078250) + 1(15.9949146) + 1(34.9688527)\n= 144.0000000 + 15.1173750 + 15.9949146 + 34.9688527\n= 210.0811423 (off by about 0.995)\n\nAnd C\u2081\u2082H\u2081\u2086OCl:\nC\u2081\u2082H\u2081\u2086OCl = 12(12.0000000) + 16(1.0078250) + 1(15.9949146) + 1(34.9688527)\n= 144.0000000 + 16.1252000 + 15.9949146 + 34.9688527\n= 211.0889673 (off by about 0.013)\n\nThe closest match appears to be **C\u2081\u2082H\u2081\u2086OCl** with a calculated mass of 211.0889673 compared to the observed 211.07639.\n\nHowever, let me also verify the isotope pattern. For one Cl atom:\n- \u00b3\u2075Cl: 75.76%\n- \u00b3\u2077Cl: 24.24%\n\nThe M+2 peak should be about 24.24/75.76 = 32% of the M peak, which matches the observed pattern (213.07369 has intensity 32.9% relative to 211.07639 at 100%).\n\nTherefore, the molecular formula is **C\u2081\u2082H\u2081\u2086OCl**.\n\nFinal Answer: C12H16OCl"
